 <p>This guide takes you from a blank machine to a working network in about ten minutes. Everything you set up here can be changed later.</p>
 <h2 id="what-you-need">What you need</h2>
 <ul>
 <li>A small computer with at least two wired network ports. It becomes your firewall, DNS server and DHCP server.</li>
 <li>The Gatehouse installer image, written to a USB stick.</li>
 <li>Your modem or provider's cable, and a switch or a computer for your own network.</li>
+<li>If you want Wi-Fi, a separate access point or Wi-Fi router plugged into your own network. Gatehouse does not include wireless support. It has no Wi-Fi drivers or firmware, and a Wi-Fi card in the machine is ignored. See Wi-Fi and wireless in the Networks help.</li>
 </ul>
 <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
