 <p>Gatehouse is built so that a wrong setting cannot lock you out for good. This page lists the ways back, from the easiest.</p>
 <h2 id="a-change-went-wrong-and-you-can-still-see-the-console">A change went wrong and you can still see the console</h2>
 <p>Every network and firewall change you apply starts a 60-second countdown. If you can still reach the console, the change is kept on its own. If you cannot, everything goes back by itself after the minute. To go back sooner, press <strong>Undo now</strong> on the countdown.</p>
@@ -21,4 +21,4 @@
 <h2 id="the-internet-is-down">The internet is down</h2>
 <p>Open <strong>Overview</strong> or <strong>Internet</strong>. Each connection shows what is wrong in words: <strong>No link</strong> means check the cable or modem, <strong>No internet</strong> means the modem is answering but the provider is not. Restart the modem first. If you have two connections, Gatehouse uses the other one on its own.</p>
 <h2 id="last-resort">Last resort</h2>
-<p>Under <strong>Settings, Backup &amp; recovery</strong>, <strong>Reset network settings</strong> puts networks, firewall rules, port forwards, DHCP, DNS names and lists, VPNs and Wi-Fi back to a clean start, and keeps your accounts, sign-in settings, update settings and console port. <strong>Factory reset</strong> erases everything and opens the setup wizard again. Both save a copy of your settings first, which you can download, and ask for your authenticator code if you use one, or your password.</p><p class="back"><a href="../">Back to the console</a></p></main></body></html>
