+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Routes - Gatehouse help</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="help.css"></head><body><nav aria-label="Help chapters"><a href="./" class="home">Help</a><a href="getting-started.html">Getting started</a><a href="recovery.html">If you are locked out</a><a href="overview.html">Overview</a><a href="internet.html">Internet</a><a href="networks.html">Networks</a><a href="dns.html">DNS</a><a href="dhcp.html">DHCP</a><a href="firewall.html">Firewall</a><a href="protection.html">Protection</a><a href="services.html">Services</a><a href="vpn.html">VPN</a><a href="routes.html" aria-current="page">Routes</a><a href="profiles.html">Profiles</a><a href="devices.html">Devices &amp; access</a><a href="logs.html">Logs</a><a href="diagnostics.html">Diagnostics</a><a href="settings.html">Settings</a><a href="reference.html">Reference</a><a href="ease-of-use.html">How easy is it?</a></nav><main><h1 id="routes">Routes</h1>
 <h2 id="what-it-is-for">What it is for</h2>
 <p>Send some traffic through a VPN by rule: everything from certain devices, or only some destinations.</p>
 <p><img src="img/routes.png" alt="The routes page, shown with no data yet" loading="lazy"></p>
