-<h2 id="what-it-is-for">What it is for</h2>
-<p>Use a Wi-Fi card in the machine to broadcast a network, or to join another network such as a hotspot.</p>
-<p><img src="img/wifi.png" alt="The wifi page, shown with no data yet" loading="lazy"></p>
-<p>The picture is an example from a new, empty box; yours will show your own devices and numbers.</p>
-<h2 id="what-is-on-the-page">What is on the page</h2>
-<ul>
-<li>One card per Wi-Fi adapter. <strong>What should this card do?</strong> offers <strong>Broadcast a Wi-Fi network</strong> or <strong>Join a Wi-Fi network</strong>.</li>
-<li>To broadcast: <strong>Network name</strong>, <strong>Password</strong>, <strong>Speed band</strong> (<strong>5 GHz</strong> is faster, <strong>2.4 GHz</strong> reaches farther), <strong>Channel</strong>, <strong>Country this device is in</strong>, and <strong>Who will use this Wi-Fi?</strong> (<strong>My own devices</strong>, <strong>Same network as wired</strong>, <strong>Guests</strong> or <strong>Smart-home gadgets</strong>). <strong>Allow WPA3</strong> and <strong>Hide the network name</strong> are options.</li>
-<li>To join: <strong>Look for networks</strong>, pick one, enter its password. <strong>Forget network</strong> removes a saved one.</li>
-<li><strong>Keep the card awake</strong> and <strong>Restart the card automatically if it stops working</strong> help cards that stop answering to save power.</li>
-<li><strong>Wi-Fi report</strong> lists what a card heard nearby.</li>
-</ul>
-<h2 id="common-tasks">Common tasks</h2>
-<ol>
-<li>Make a guest Wi-Fi: choose <strong>Broadcast a Wi-Fi network</strong>, name it, set a password, choose <strong>Guests</strong>, <strong>Save</strong>, <strong>Review and apply</strong>.</li>
-<li>Share the password: use the printable join card, which shows a QR code.</li>
-<li>Join a hotspot as your internet: choose <strong>Join a Wi-Fi network</strong> and pick it.</li>
-</ol>
-<h2 id="example">Example</h2>
-<p>Broadcast "Home" on 5 GHz for <strong>My own devices</strong>, and "Home guests" on 2.4 GHz for <strong>Guests</strong>.</p>
-<h2 id="if-something-goes-wrong">If something goes wrong</h2>
-<p><strong>This card cannot broadcast here</strong> means the card or the country setting does not allow it. Check <strong>Country this device is in</strong>. If the card stops answering, turn on <strong>Turn off power saving</strong>.</p><p class="back"><a href="../">Back to the console</a></p></main></body></html>
